            <div xml:id="d114">

                <pb facs="0291" n="195" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg195"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">362.115 St 21/432: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Whitehouse</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-10-02T14:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 2,
                                1926—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 2—10:55
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>371. [From Hill.] H–152. Department’s H–80<anchor n="18" xml:id="d114-f1"/>
                    received while in Reparation Commission meeting today.</p>
                <p>Commission decided to attribute tankers to Great Britain and indicated
                    willingness that that Government should arrange with us for delivery. British
                    delegation believes British Board of Trade will act. I will confirm this.
                    Hill.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitehouse</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
